1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,344
I’m Selçuk, building in Istanbul.

2
00:00:02,344 --> 00:00:06,094
Earthquake preparation includes the
things inside a room.

3
00:00:06,094 --> 00:00:12,188
RiskLens connects a visible finding to
its evidence and a practical next step.

4
00:00:12,188 --> 00:00:15,000
This room is synthetic, from Hypersim.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,200
I built this for people preparing their own homes,
under the Build for Your World theme.

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:23,400
You start by recording or uploading
a short video of one room.

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:27,600
If you'd rather not share your home,
the sample report opens instantly,

8
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:31,400
or you can run the sample
through Meta's models again,

9
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:35,000
as I do here.

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,179
Muse Spark first
selects objects worth examining.

11
00:00:39,179 --> 00:00:43,358
SAM tracks candidate
objects through the video.

12
00:00:43,358 --> 00:00:49,328
Spark then reviews sampled frames
with those objects marked, connecting

13
00:00:49,328 --> 00:00:52,313
findings to specific visual evidence.

14
00:00:52,313 --> 00:00:57,687
The report separates observations
from details that need checking.

15
00:00:57,687 --> 00:01:04,851
A connection hidden behind furniture is
unknown, not proof that the furniture

16
00:01:04,851 --> 00:01:06,045
is unsecured.

17
00:01:06,045 --> 00:01:13,209
Waiting is shortened here; the audit
trail records the actual processing time

18
00:01:13,209 --> 00:01:15,000
and model cost.

19
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,500
For a finding, RiskLens
looks up relevant FEMA guidance.

20
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,000
Suggestions link to sections
actually returned by that lookup.

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,500
If the source check
fails, actionable instructions are withheld.

22
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:34,500
These links show what the model
read; they are not expert approval.

23
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,500
Installation conditions still
need appropriate assessment.

24
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:44,500
The aim is to make the next
question and the supporting evidence easy to

25
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:45,000
understand.

26
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,326
Comparison also needs evidence.

27
00:01:47,326 --> 00:01:53,140
Uploading the original video cannot
demonstrate a new physical change.

28
00:01:53,140 --> 00:01:58,372
That check uses the
file hash, not model perception.

29
00:01:58,372 --> 00:02:04,767
We also test unchanged rendered
footage and a different synthetic room.

30
00:02:04,767 --> 00:02:09,419
Those are limited regression
controls, not real-world before-and-after

31
00:02:09,419 --> 00:02:10,000
validation.

32
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,729
The evaluation compares Spark-only and
the full pipeline on five synthetic

33
00:02:15,729 --> 00:02:18,333
scenes previously used in development.

34
00:02:18,333 --> 00:02:25,104
We record failures, completion, time and
cost, and repeat the main scene to

35
00:02:25,104 --> 00:02:26,146
expose variation.

36
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:30,312
More findings do not
automatically mean better accuracy.

37
00:02:30,312 --> 00:02:34,479
Human correctness review and
positive physical-change validation remain

38
00:02:34,479 --> 00:02:35,000
unfinished.

39
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,581
RiskLens is a visual screening prototype,
not a building inspection or safety

40
00:02:40,581 --> 00:02:41,047
certificate.

41
00:02:41,047 --> 00:02:47,558
The public example is ready to explore,
and the code documents what was built

42
00:02:47,558 --> 00:02:48,953
during the hackathon.

43
00:02:48,953 --> 00:02:54,535
Find the evidence, understand the uncertainty,
and decide what needs a closer

44
00:02:54,535 --> 00:02:55,000
look.
